# Bot-led groups (docs/BOT-LED-GROUPS.md, change 9): what the gamebot leader of a party that invited the player says.
# Short and lowercase, the way 2003 leaders typed. Only BotLedGroups asks for these (flag lead_call, which no bot has on
# its own), so ambient group talk never says them. {destination} is where the group is or meets, {camp} what it hunts.
# A line never promises what the server will not do: nobody is summoned, ported or given money. New writing.

# ---- lead_invite: the tell before the group invite box (unasked) ----
@kind tell
@topic lead_invite
@who *
@needs lead_call
@invites ask
lf 1 more for {monsters} in {destination}, want in?
[need|lf] one more for {monsters}, [want in|interested]?
got a spot open, {monsters} in {destination}. [want in|you up for it]?
hey, we have room for one more. {monsters} in {destination}, [want to come|you in]?
forming up for {monsters}, could use you. want an inv?

# ---- lead_invite_asked: the player asked (/lfg, a tell) ----
@topic lead_invite_asked
@invites none
[got|have] room, sending [you an|an] inv
sure, inv coming
yep, [sending|incoming] inv
we have a spot, inv sent

# ---- lead_afk_let_go: the group moved on after 30 minutes away (tell) ----
@topic lead_afk_let_go
@invites none
had to move on, send me a tell when you are back
we went on without you, [send me a tell|tell me] when you are back and we can [regroup|sort it out]

# ---- In the group (/group) ----
@kind group
@who *
@needs in_player_group,bot_leads,lead_call
@invites none
@topic lead_welcome
welcome! meet up at {destination}
[welcome|hey], we meet at {destination}
welcome aboard, meeting at {destination}, see you there
@topic lead_welcome_out
welcome! we are at {destination}, come find us
[welcome|hey], we are out at {destination}, [follow me if you are close|come find us]
@topic lead_wait
still at {destination}, waiting on you
we are at {destination} [whenever you are ready|still]
waiting at {destination}, no rush
@topic lead_going_on
heading on to {camp}, catch up when you can
going on to {camp}, meet us there, spot is saved
moving on to {camp}, [your spot is saved|we saved your spot]
@topic lead_where
where u at?
[where are you|where u at], need directions?
you still with us?
@topic lead_afk_hold
everyone med, waiting on our last one
[holding|hold up] a sec, everyone med
@topic lead_move
moving to {camp}
[ok|alright], heading to {camp}
on to {camp}, [stay close|follow me]
@topic lead_break
thats it for me, good group all
gotta call it, [ty all|thanks all], good group
@topic lead_player_left
lost one, we carry on
[ok|alright], carrying on without them

# ---- B2: the handover (docs/BOT-LED-GROUPS.md, "Taking the lead") ----
# lead_handover: the leader, as the player types /lead. lead_take: the gamebot the player handed the lead to (/lead bot,
# /makeleader). lead_last_bot: the last gamebot of the party, just before the "do you want to lead?" box.
@topic lead_handover
all yours, we follow you
[ok|sure], your lead
[all yours|your group now], lead on
k new lead, everyone follow
@topic lead_take
ok i'll lead, finding us a camp near here
[sure|ok], i got it. looking for a camp around here
i'll take it, give me a sec to find a spot nearby
@topic lead_last_bot
just us two left, want to lead?
[well|hm], it's just us now. you want to lead?
everyone bailed, your call

# ---- B3: the raid leader (docs/BOT-LED-GROUPS.md, "Raid leaders") ----
# lead_raid_welcome: the leader of the raid party the player was seated in. {destination} is the raid's muster town.
@topic lead_raid_welcome
welcome, we wait at {destination} until the raid leaves
[welcome|hey], we muster at {destination}, see you there
glad you came, meet us at {destination} before we head out

# ---- B4: the leader's pull call (it replaces the generic "inc" for that pull: one line per pull) ----
@topic lead_pull
pulling
[pulling|incoming], get ready
inc, on me
inc, [stay on me|watch for adds]
pulling, [healers|everyone] ready?
[here it comes|here we go]
incoming, [assist me|on my target]
one coming, [get set|be ready]
[ok|k] pulling, [hold aggro|tank it]
inc inc

# ---- B4: the natural break (bags nearly full, or the task's last minutes) ----
# lead_sell: the call before the last pull. lead_town: the goodbye once that pull is over and the party ends to sell.
@topic lead_sell
last pull then town
[bags full|bags are full], last pull then we sell
one more pull, then town to sell
[ok|alright], last one then [town|we go sell]
@topic lead_town
ok town to sell, good group all
[thats it|done], heading to town to sell, [ty all|thanks all]
selling up, [good group|nice run] everyone
bags full, calling it, [ty for the group|thanks for the group]

# ---- B4: the leader's search for a replacement (the ask itself goes to /lfg, lead_lf_more below) ----
@topic lead_recruited
got someone coming, hang tight
[found|got] one, they are on the way
replacement on the way, [hold here|med up while we wait]
@topic lead_recruit_none
no luck finding anyone, we carry on as we are
[nobody|no one] bit, we keep going short
cant find one, we manage without
@topic lead_recruit_end
couldnt find anyone, gonna call it here
[no luck|nobody around], calling it, [ty all|thanks all]
cant run without one, done for now
# ---- B4: lead_lf_more, the leader's /lfg ask for a replacement ({need}: "a healer", "a tank", "dps"; {camp}: what it hunts) ----
@kind lfg
@needs in_group,lead_call
@invites none
@topic lead_lf_more
lf 1 more, need {need} for {camp}
[lf1m|lf 1m] {need}, {camp}
lf 1 more at {camp}, need {need}, pst
need {need} at {camp}, [send a tell|pst]
{camp} group lf {need}, [quick xp|steady pulls]

# lead_raid_invite: the raid leader's one tell to a level-50 player before the box. {raid} is the encounter's name.
@kind tell
@topic lead_raid_invite
@who *
@needs lead_call
@invites none
forming for {raid} at {destination}. want a spot?
[forming|putting together] a raid for {raid} at {destination}, [want in|you in]?
{raid} raid forming at {destination}, we could use you. want a spot?
